{title: 358 - Far and Near the Fields Are Teeming}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #358 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 358}
{meta: category Christian Church - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Far and near the [Bb]fields are teeming [F]with the sheaves of rip[G7]ened [C]grain;
[F]Far and near their [Bb]gold is gleaming [F]O'er the sun[Bb]ny [F]slope [C7]and [F]plain.
[F]Lord of harvest, [C7]send forth reapers! [F]Hear us Lord, to [Bb]The[F]e we [C]cry;
[F]Send them now the [Bb]sheaves to gather, [F]Ere the har[Bb]vest[F]time [C7]pass [F]by.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[F]Lord [Bb]of [F]harvest, [G7]send [C]forth reapers!
[F][Bb]Hear [F]us [Bb]Lord,to [F]Thee [C7]we [F]cry;
[F]Send [C7]them [F]now [Bb]the [F]sheaves [C]to gather,
[F][Bb]Ere [F]the [Bb][F]harvest-time [C7]pass [F]by.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Send [Bb]them [F]forth with [G7]morn's [C]first beaming,
[F][Bb]Send [F]them [Bb]in [F]the [C7]noon-tides's [F]glare;
[F]When [C7]the [F]sun's [Bb]last [F]rays [C]are streaming,
[F][Bb]bid [F][Bb]them [F][C7]gather [F]everywhere.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]O [Bb]thou, [F]whom thy [G7]Lord [C]is sending,
[F][Bb]gather [F]now [Bb]the [F]sheaves [C7]of [F]gold;
[F][C7]Heavenward [F]then [Bb]at [F]evening [C]wending
[F][Bb]Thou [F]shalt [Bb]come [F]with [C7]joy [F]untold.
{end_of_verse}
